# Agent chats run on a host that declares `sessions`: the server's own, or
# a worker's for another server (docs/proposals/2026-11-13-what-each-machine-is.md).
# Before that role it was `origin`, and a host that declares `origin` with
# MEDIA_HEADLESS on is still taken to have `sessions` (setup.effective_roles).
# Only once the feature is switched on there: without MEDIA_HEADLESS in
# agent-media.env the service is skipped, never installed and idle.
requires: sessions
requires-env: MEDIA_HEADLESS
